This directory contains a frozen SGLang Python source snapshot and ToolSlack
native KV integration used by the dense Qwen3-8B experiment.

SGLang upstream: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang
Upstream license: Apache License 2.0; see LICENSE.
The original source copyright and SPDX notices are retained, including notices
for code derived from Qwen, Hugging Face Transformers, and other upstream works.
No separate upstream top-level NOTICE file was present in the inspected checkout.

The snapshot includes custom exact-prefix lease, asynchronous native HiCache
transfer, service-profile binding, and admitted-request headroom integration.
The corresponding modules and their hashes are recorded in SOURCE_MANIFEST.json.
This notice describes the snapshot; it does not establish a public Git base
commit for the fork or certify compatibility with a newly installed GPU runtime.

The original source snapshot was frozen for provenance. Artifact packaging changes
such as modified-file notices should be recorded separately and should regenerate
the distributed source manifest and service-profile binding.

Artifact modification notice: project-specific KV namespace identifiers and associated module filenames were changed consistently to ToolSlack for anonymous review. Local packaging metadata was added for installation; upstream copyright headers remain.
